<title>USA: Penederm wins patent suit against Alzo.</title>
<headline>Penederm wins patent suit against Alzo.</headline>
<dateline>FOSTER CITY, Calif. 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Penederm Inc Tuesday said the it has won a patent infringement suit against Alzo Inc, of New Jersey, in respect to three Penederm TopiCare Delivery Compound patents.</p>
<p>According to the ruling of the U.S. district court in San Francisco, Alzo has been permanently enjoined from selling six cosmetic ingredient products that infringe on Penederm's three patents, the company said. Alzo must also pay a portion of Penederm's legal fees related to the case.</p>
<p>Penederm filed the patent infringement suit in 1994.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk +1 212 859 1610))</p>
